1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,710
Last time, we learnt that a magnet is usually made of iron

2
00:00:03,730 --> 00:00:06,420
or steel, and it attracts the steel pin.

3
00:00:06,870 --> 00:00:10,120
But it ignored the copper wire, and copper is a metal!

4
00:00:11,382 --> 00:00:13,682
We rinsed two empty cans for recycling.

5
00:00:13,885 --> 00:00:16,335
A little snail is hiding in this video.

6
00:00:16,615 --> 00:00:17,815
Can you spot it?

7
00:00:17,945 --> 00:00:19,445
Look low, where it is wet!

8
00:00:19,568 --> 00:00:21,408
Lock in first with your fingers.

9
00:00:21,678 --> 00:00:23,508
One finger for every point.

10
00:00:24,095 --> 00:00:25,395
Today you'll learn:

11
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:26,950
Not all metals.

12
00:00:27,153 --> 00:00:28,843
How magnets interact.

13
00:00:29,039 --> 00:00:30,569
Test, do not guess.

14
00:00:32,168 --> 00:00:33,048
Round one.

15
00:00:33,358 --> 00:00:35,068
Which can will the magnet pull?

16
00:00:35,358 --> 00:00:36,678
One, the drink can.

17
00:00:36,978 --> 00:00:38,368
Two, the food tin.

18
00:00:38,668 --> 00:00:39,678
Three, both.

19
00:00:39,958 --> 00:00:41,318
Show me your fingers.

20
00:00:46,790 --> 00:00:47,770
Locked in!

21
00:00:47,898 --> 00:00:48,498
Three!

22
00:00:48,868 --> 00:00:52,598
They are both metal cans, and they are both shiny and silver.

23
00:00:52,646 --> 00:00:53,526
Two.

24
00:00:53,686 --> 00:00:56,646
At home, a fridge magnet held on to a food tin like

25
00:00:56,666 --> 00:00:57,276
this.

26
00:00:57,496 --> 00:00:58,816
I tested it.

27
00:00:58,864 --> 00:00:59,494
Two!

28
00:00:59,634 --> 00:01:02,804
Dad says drink cans like this are made of aluminium.

29
00:01:03,044 --> 00:01:05,414
And aluminium is not iron or steel!

30
00:01:05,836 --> 00:01:07,256
Be an aluminium can!

31
00:01:07,596 --> 00:01:08,586
Shrink down.

32
00:01:08,856 --> 00:01:09,796
Quietly.

33
00:01:12,079 --> 00:01:15,059
You are an empty drink can, made of aluminium.

34
00:01:15,919 --> 00:01:16,729
Clunk!

35
00:01:17,499 --> 00:01:19,909
You drop into the blue recycling bin.

36
00:01:20,430 --> 00:01:22,920
A truck takes you to a recycling plant.

37
00:01:23,690 --> 00:01:28,070
You ride a moving belt, with steel food tins and plastic bottles.

38
00:01:28,586 --> 00:01:31,156
Above the belt hangs a giant magnet.

39
00:01:31,966 --> 00:01:32,716
Clang!

40
00:01:33,506 --> 00:01:35,706
The steel tins jump up onto it.

41
00:01:36,225 --> 00:01:37,635
But you roll right on.

42
00:01:38,445 --> 00:01:41,965
The magnet does not pull you, even though you are a metal.

43
00:01:43,615 --> 00:01:46,205
The answer is two: the steel food tin!

44
00:01:46,465 --> 00:01:48,045
Did you show two fingers?

45
00:01:48,285 --> 00:01:49,725
Put one finger up!

46
00:01:49,853 --> 00:01:52,823
But the drink can and the copper wire are both metal.

47
00:01:52,903 --> 00:01:54,863
Why does the magnet ignore them?

48
00:01:55,518 --> 00:01:56,648
Look closer.

49
00:01:57,258 --> 00:02:01,358
Basil's magnet passes every object on our table, and not one of

50
00:02:01,378 --> 00:02:02,324
them moves.

51
00:02:02,344 --> 00:02:06,354
These objects are made of non-magnetic materials.

52
00:02:06,876 --> 00:02:08,006
Non means not.

53
00:02:08,106 --> 00:02:12,406
Non-magnetic materials are the ones a magnet does not attract, like wood,

54
00:02:12,426 --> 00:02:13,921
glass and plastic!

55
00:02:13,941 --> 00:02:15,511
Here is the surprise.

56
00:02:15,641 --> 00:02:19,764
Copper and aluminium are metals, but they are non-magnetic too!

57
00:02:19,784 --> 00:02:21,694
So being a metal is not enough!

58
00:02:21,764 --> 00:02:25,034
Only some metals, like iron and steel, are magnetic.

59
00:02:27,735 --> 00:02:28,985
Say it with me!

60
00:02:29,695 --> 00:02:34,605
Objects that are not attracted to magnets are made of non-magnetic materials.

61
00:02:35,195 --> 00:02:40,425
Non-magnetic materials include ceramic, fabric, glass, plastic, rubber and wood.

62
00:02:41,055 --> 00:02:45,095
Metals such as aluminium and copper are also non-magnetic.

63
00:02:48,525 --> 00:02:49,425
Showdown!

64
00:02:49,735 --> 00:02:50,865
Double points.

65
00:02:51,135 --> 00:02:53,325
Basil's homework has one mistake.

66
00:02:53,605 --> 00:02:55,365
Line one, two, or three?

67
00:02:55,665 --> 00:02:57,145
Show me with your fingers.

68
00:02:57,203 --> 00:03:00,283
One: the iron nail is attracted, so it is magnetic.

69
00:03:00,473 --> 00:03:04,353
Two: the wooden ruler is not attracted, so it is non-magnetic.

70
00:03:04,613 --> 00:03:07,543
Three: the foil is shiny and grey, like steel, so it is

71
00:03:07,563 --> 00:03:08,573
magnetic.

72
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:15,160
Locked in!

73
00:03:15,288 --> 00:03:15,888
Three!

74
00:03:16,238 --> 00:03:17,998
We cannot tell by looking.

75
00:03:18,038 --> 00:03:22,018
The magnet did not attract the foil, so the foil is non-magnetic.

76
00:03:23,292 --> 00:03:24,382
Three fingers?

77
00:03:24,622 --> 00:03:26,552
Put up two more on your score hand!

78
00:03:26,902 --> 00:03:29,262
Our new theme is called Interactions.

79
00:03:29,522 --> 00:03:32,068
When you push a swing, it moves away from you.

80
00:03:32,088 --> 00:03:34,908
Magnets interact with other objects too.

81
00:03:36,348 --> 00:03:38,818
Interact means one thing acts on another.

82
00:03:39,028 --> 00:03:41,728
The magnet pulls the pin, and the pin moves!

83
00:03:42,379 --> 00:03:43,529
Look closer.

84
00:03:44,119 --> 00:03:48,070
Bring the magnet near each object, and watch how they interact.

85
00:03:48,090 --> 00:03:53,100
One of the ways to classify these materials is to observe how

86
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:55,260
they interact with a magnet.

87
00:03:56,384 --> 00:03:59,114
To classify is to sort things into groups.

88
00:03:59,134 --> 00:04:03,344
The magnet sorts them into two groups: magnetic and non-magnetic!

89
00:04:06,049 --> 00:04:07,209
Say it with me!

90
00:04:07,918 --> 00:04:12,388
A magnet can interact with objects that are made of magnetic materials.

91
00:04:15,148 --> 00:04:16,253
Say it with us!

92
00:04:16,913 --> 00:04:18,068
Iron and steel?

93
00:04:18,493 --> 00:04:19,476
Magnetic!

94
00:04:23,313 --> 00:04:24,873
Copper and aluminium?

95
00:04:24,893 --> 00:04:26,066
Non-magnetic!

96
00:04:29,713 --> 00:04:30,880
Do not guess!

97
00:04:31,293 --> 00:04:32,846
Test it with a magnet!

98
00:04:36,868 --> 00:04:38,338
Show me your score hand!

99
00:04:38,618 --> 00:04:39,668
More than one?

100
00:04:39,968 --> 00:04:41,328
You beat the Buddies.

101
00:04:41,628 --> 00:04:42,688
Three fingers?

102
00:04:42,958 --> 00:04:43,968
High five!

103
00:04:44,473 --> 00:04:45,903
Did you spot the snail?

104
00:04:46,193 --> 00:04:48,553
It was on a wet leaf of the potted plant!

105
00:04:48,690 --> 00:04:49,980
Here is a fun fact!

106
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,730
Deep in the sea lives a snail with iron in its shell.

107
00:04:52,750 --> 00:04:54,580
A magnet can attract this snail!

108
00:04:54,709 --> 00:04:55,989
Tell someone at home!

109
00:04:56,878 --> 00:04:59,668
Next time: two ring magnets on a pencil!

110
00:04:59,918 --> 00:05:03,458
The top one floats in mid-air, with no glue and no string.

111
00:05:03,738 --> 00:05:04,868
What holds it up?

112
00:05:05,258 --> 00:05:06,348
One, a pull.

113
00:05:06,648 --> 00:05:07,668
Two, a push.

114
00:05:07,948 --> 00:05:09,268
Lock in your answer!

115
00:05:09,540 --> 00:05:11,740
Let's read today's key words together!

116
00:05:12,030 --> 00:05:12,790
Ready?

117
00:05:13,077 --> 00:05:14,757
Non-magnetic materials.

118
00:05:16,870 --> 00:05:17,720
Interact.

119
00:05:19,250 --> 00:05:20,270
Classify.

120
00:05:21,819 --> 00:05:22,759
Well done!

121
00:05:23,741 --> 00:05:24,842
Say it with us!

122
00:05:25,642 --> 00:05:26,392
Ready?

123
00:05:26,516 --> 00:05:27,176
One!

124
00:05:27,516 --> 00:05:28,216
two!

125
00:05:28,521 --> 00:05:29,696
Now you know!
